-- title:
--   A coefficient complete DVR for the completed K-node ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a level $N \neq 0$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$; fix modular polynomial data for $q$ (a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ annihilating the pair of $q$-expansions) together with the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \equiv (X^q - Y)(X - Y^q) \bmod q$, integrality of the two Hecke $\bar\alpha$- and $\bar\beta$-maps at level $N$, a place specialization $P$ of the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-modular function field of level $N$ along $red$, and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$. Assume $q \nmid N$ and that $red\,c = 0$ exactly when $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $w$ a place of the level-$N$ modular function field over $k$, i.e. a proper valuation subring containing $k$ which is a principal ideal ring. Write $\mathcal{O} = R.nodeIntegersOver\ K\ w$ for the subring of the level-$Nq$ field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ consisting of those $f$ lying in $R.nodeIntegers\ w$ whose Laurent series lies in the field over $K$, and assume $\mathcal{O}$ is local and Noetherian. Let $B = A \cap K$ (the intersection of $A$ with $K$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and $c_w : B \to \mathcal{O}$ the map sending $o$ to the constant $o$. Assume every $g \in \mathcal{O}$ satisfies $g - c_w(o)$ non-unit for some $o \in B$, and let $\varpi \in B$ be such that, for $d \in B$, the restriction of $red$ to $B$ kills $d$ exactly when $\varpi \mid d$. Then there exist a type $W$ carrying a commutative ring structure making it a domain, a discrete valuation ring complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology, an irreducible $\pi \in W$, and a ring homomorphism $\sigma$ from $W$ to the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}$ at its maximal ideal, such that $\sigma(\pi)$ is the image of $c_w(\varpi)$ in the completion, and every $f \in \mathcal{O}$ has its image in the completion congruent to $\sigma(o)$, for some $o \in W$, modulo the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   This supplies the coefficient data $(W,\pi,\sigma)$ — a complete discrete valuation ring with uniformiser mapping to the constant $\varpi$ and surjective on residues of the completed $K$-node ring — on which the local models of the node of $X_0(Nq)$ in characteristic $q$ are built. It is used by the statements producing crossing presentations, node annuli and component charts at such a place.
